Laws 2025, First Special Session chapter 3, article 18, section 3 by Laws 2026, chapter 95, article 4, section 42

Sec. 3. DIRECTION TO COMMISSIONER; INDIAN HEALTH SERVICE ENCOUNTER RATE.
The commissioner of human services must submit a state plan amendment to the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services authorizing housing services as a new service category eligible for reimbursement at the outpatient per-day rate approved by the Indian Health Service. This reimbursement is limited to services provided by facilities of the Indian Health Service and facilities owned or operated by a Tribe or Tribal organization. For the purposes of this section, "housing services" means housing stabilization services as described in Minnesota Statutes, section 256B.051, subdivision 5, paragraphs (a) to (d).
